  "usage_note": "Use **on** before a day: *on Monday*. *On Mondays* means every Monday. There is no preposition before **next**, **last**, **this**, or **every**: *next Monday*. In American English, **on** is often left out in speech: *See you Monday*. The short written form is **Mon.**",
